;; The KIT's own secrets allowances: a hit of the security pack's secrets scan over the KIT's history
;; that is known not to be a secret, with the reason. `bb tag-check` passes this file to the scan
;; (`--routes`), and so does the KIT's own security review's first scan (the kit-session skill); an
;; allowed hit is a warn that names its reason, never a pass that says nothing. The scan matches an
;; entry by file and rule, not by line: an entry allows that rule anywhere in the file, so it names
;; a test file, never a source file. Added only with the person's word, the reason written here.
{:secrets-allowed
 [{:file "harness/test/harness/tools/toolchain_env_test.clj"
   :rule :url-credentials
   :reason "the .env loader's test values: a database URL whose user, password and host are one letter each, no credential (plan 7.0, 2026-11-02; the person: \"go, allow file\")"}]}
